00:12:20,610 --> 00:12:23,020
In order to preserve your friendship

270
00:12:23,020 --> 00:12:25,080
you and Howard made a pinky swear

271
00:12:25,080 --> 00:12:27,410
that neither of you would attempt to woo her.

272
00:12:27,910 --> 00:12:29,460
I had a patty melt.

273
00:12:30,620 --> 00:12:32,490
Okay   fine   I betrayed Howard.

274
00:12:32,490 --> 00:12:34,420
- And Raj.  - All right   and Raj.

275
00:12:34,420 --> 00:12:35,500
And me.

276
00:12:36,090 --> 00:12:37,650
You?

277
00:12:37,820 --> 00:12:39,430
Violation of the Roommate Agreement's

278
00:12:39,430 --> 00:12:41,830
overnight guest notification clause.

279
00:12:41,830 --> 00:12:44,700
Okay   fine   I-I'm a horrible human being.

280
00:12:44,700 --> 00:12:46,800
I'm the Darth Vader of Pasadena.

281
00:12:46,800 --> 00:12:49,500
You're far too short to be Darth Vader.

282
00:12:50,440 --> 00:12:52,880
At best you might be a turncoat Ewok.

283
00:12:53,340 --> 00:12:56,740
My point is: Priya's gone and it would be much better

284
00:12:56,740 --> 00:12:59,450
if no one else found out about us.

285
00:13:00,280 --> 00:13:02,310
You mean you want me to keep a secret?

286
00:13:02,320 --> 00:13:03,350
Yes.

287
00:13:03,350 --> 00:13:05,020
You know I can't keep a secret.

288
00:13:05,020 --> 00:13:06,090
You can if you try.

289
00:13:06,090 --> 00:13:07,320
Think about it this way:

290
00:13:07,320 --> 00:13:10,220
um   if I were Batman and you were Alfred

291
00:13:10,220 --> 00:13:12,160
you'd keep that secret   right?

292
00:13:12,390 --> 00:13:14,960
Why do you get to be Batman?

293
00:13:14,960 --> 00:13:17,100
Because Batman has the secret.

294
00:13:17,100 --> 00:13:18,930
Alfred has secrets   too.

295
00:13:18,930 --> 00:13:20,500
- Like what?  - Alfred knows

296
00:13:20,500 --> 00:13:22,170
that Barbara Gordon is Batgirl.

297
00:13:22,800 --> 00:13:24,300
Which I've now just told to Batman.

298
00:13:24,300 --> 00:13:25,990
See   I cannot keep a secret.

299
00:13:30,110 --> 00:13:31,240
Ta-dah!

300
00:13:31,850 --> 00:13:32,880
What?

301
00:13:33,300 --> 00:13:34,220
Ta-dah.

302
00:13:35,320 --> 00:13:36,250
It's short for...

303
00:13:36,250 --> 00:13:38,220
Da-da-da-da! ?

304
00:13:39,370 --> 00:13:40,850
Kind of busy here   Sheldon.

305
00:13:40,850 --> 00:13:42,190
I know   that's why I shortened it.

306
00:13:44,750 --> 00:13:45,720
What do you want?

307
00:13:45,730 --> 00:13:49,430
I came to go over your alibi for last night.

308
00:13:49,430 --> 00:13:50,860
What alibi?

309
00:13:50,860 --> 00:13:54,130
You've asked me to lie on your behalf   and as you know

310
00:13:54,130 --> 00:13:57,140
I am deeply uncomfortable with impromptu dishonesty

311
00:13:57,140 --> 00:14:00,470
so I've provided you with an ironclad alibi.

312
00:14:00,470 --> 00:14:03,140
You couldn't have spent last night with Priya

313
00:14:03,140 --> 00:14:05,210
because you were with another woman.

314
00:14:05,210 --> 00:14:07,450
Oh   I'm so sure I'm gonna regret this

315
00:14:07,450 --> 00:14:10,550
but who was I with?

316
00:14:10,550 --> 00:14:14,650
The fun-loving and morally loose Miss Maggie McGarry.

317
00:14:14,650 --> 00:14:16,090
Oh   God.

318
00:14:16,090 --> 00:14:18,040
You met her at Pasadena's most popular

319
00:14:18,040 --> 00:14:20,520
Irish watering hole   Lucky Baldwin's

320
00:14:20,520 --> 00:14:22,630
where Maggie spends her nights tending bar

321
00:14:22,630 --> 00:14:25,830
with a head full of curls and a heart full of dreams.

322
00:14:25,830 --> 00:14:29,940
"Leonard   call me if you are interested in coitus.

323
00:14:31,070 --> 00:14:33,570
Sincerely   Maggie McGarry."

324
00:14:33,570 --> 00:14:34,870
And if anyone were

325
00:14:34,870 --> 00:14:39,780
to actually call that number   they will hear this.

326
00:14:39,780 --> 00:14:41,880
Top of the morning to you.

327
00:14:41,880 --> 00:14:44,050
You've reached Maggie McGarry.

328
00:14:45,250 --> 00:14:49,420
Leave a message after the wee little beep.

329
00:14:50,490 --> 00:14:51,820
It's pretty convincing   huh?

330
00:14:51,830 --> 00:14:53,090
That wasn't even a real person.

331
00:14:53,090 --> 00:14:56,360
And here is the clincher:

332
00:14:56,360 --> 00:15:01,000
a lock of Maggie's flaming auburn hair.

333
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:02,270
Where'd you get that?

334
00:15:02,270 --> 00:15:05,070
From an orangutan in the primate lab.

335
00:15:05,070 --> 00:15:06,170
An orangutan?

336
00:15:06,170 --> 00:15:09,270
Well   no one's going to run a DNA test on it   Leonard.

337
00:15:09,280 --> 00:15:11,340
Honestly   you overthink everything.

338
00:15:11,340 --> 00:15:14,650
Sheldon   I don't need an alibi.

339
00:15:14,650 --> 00:15:16,420
Nobody's going to ask about last night

340
00:15:16,420 --> 00:15:18,850
as long as you just zip your lip.

341
00:15:22,160 --> 00:15:23,460
Thank you.

342
00:15:23,460 --> 00:15:25,790
Now   don't worry   everything is going to be fine.

343
00:15:39,710 --> 00:15:39,740
Hey.

344
00:15:40,710 --> 00:15:41,970
Hey   Leonard   will you please tell Howard

345
00:15:41,980 --> 00:15:44,110
my sister has never been attracted to him?

346
00:15:44,780 --> 00:15:45,940
Come on   Raj

347
00:15:45,950 --> 00:15:47,450
how am I supposed to know

348
00:15:47,450 --> 00:15:50,680
who she is attracted to or was attracted to

349
00:15:50,680 --> 00:15:55,320
or who she might be attracted to in the future?

350
00:15:55,320 --> 00:15:57,960
And I have nothing to contribute

351
00:15:57,960 --> 00:16:00,830
to this conversation.

352
00:16:01,800 --> 00:16:03,830
Because I   too   know absolutely nothing

353
00:16:03,830 --> 00:16:06,900
about Priya's preferences in male companionship.

354
00:16:07,730 --> 00:16:10,400
And with that   I will re-zip my lip.

355
00:16:11,240 --> 00:16:13,610
Hey   so what did you guys think

356
00:16:13,610 --> 00:16:15,640
of the new episode of Caprica last night?

357
00:16:15,640 --> 00:16:16,610
I didn't see it.

358
00:16:16,610 --> 00:16:17,540
Didn't see it?

359
00:16:17,540 --> 00:16:19,140
What were you doing?

360
00:16:22,980 --> 00:16:24,080
Uh   I was out.

361
00:16:24,080 --> 00:16:25,880
What   on Caprica night?

362
00:16:25,890 --> 00:16:28,190
Yeah   I   uh   went for a drink.

363
00:16:28,190 --> 00:16:29,420
Really   you?

364
00:16:29,420 --> 00:16:32,190
Where   w-where'd you go?

365
00:16:32,190 --> 00:16:34,430
To   uh...

366
00:16:39,900 --> 00:16:42,370
Lucky Baldwin's.

367
00:16:42,370 --> 00:16:46,270
Oh   I've heard of that place.

368
00:16:46,270 --> 00:16:50,010
Isn't that Pasadena's favorite Irish watering hole?

369
00:16:50,010 --> 00:16:51,780
Yes.

370
00:16:51,780 --> 00:16:53,080
Did you meet

371
00:16:53,080 --> 00:16:54,350
anyone interesting there

372
00:16:54,350 --> 00:16:58,580
perhaps a promiscuous   redheaded barmaid?

373
00:16:58,590 --> 00:17:00,590
As a matter of fact... I-I-I-I-I can't   I can't

374
00:17:00,590 --> 00:17:02,020
I can't do it.

375
00:17:02,020 --> 00:17:04,590
Sure you can   you're doing fine   it's very believable.

376
00:17:05,530 --> 00:17:08,060
I'm sorry   Raj   but the truth is

377
00:17:08,060 --> 00:17:09,930
I was with Priya last night.

378
00:17:09,930 --> 00:17:11,130
Don't listen to him.

379
00:17:11,130 --> 00:17:12,900
He's still light-headed from all the Irish whiskey

380
00:17:12,900 --> 00:17:14,770
and pickled eggs in his system.

381
00:17:14,770 --> 00:17:16,700
What were you doing with Priya?

382
00:17:16,700 --> 00:17:17,740
I believe they engaged in coitus

383
00:17:17,740 --> 00:17:19,540
but more importantly

384
00:17:19,540 --> 00:17:21,310
if Leonard had not abandoned his story

385
00:17:21,310 --> 00:17:23,740
would you have found it plausible?

386
00:17:23,740 --> 00:17:25,280
You slept with my sister?!

387
00:17:25,280 --> 00:17:26,210
Yeah.

388
00:17:26,210 --> 00:17:28,450
How could you? We had a pact.

389
00:17:28,450 --> 00:17:30,250
Excuse me   I think "How could you? She's my sister"

390
00:17:30,250 --> 00:17:33,450
takes precedence over a five-year-old pinky swear.

391
00:17:33,450 --> 00:17:34,890
May I point out

392
00:17:34,890 --> 00:17:37,120
in a parallel universe   your friends are saying

393
00:17:37,120 --> 00:17:39,760
"Maggie McGarry-- she sounds lovely."

394
00:17:39,760 --> 00:17:43,230
Look   I-I admit it   I may have crossed a line here

395
00:17:43,230 --> 00:17:46,800
but come on   Raj   your sister is a grown woman

396
00:17:46,800 --> 00:17:49,700
and to her   I'm a forbidden piece of white chocolate.

397
00:17:49,700 --> 00:17:51,800
I don't believe it.

398
00:17:51,810 --> 00:17:53,210
This is a terrible betrayal of my trust.

399
00:17:53,210 --> 00:17:55,870
No   w-w-would it help if I told you

400
00:17:55,880 --> 00:17:59,810
that I offered her my heart   and she kind of stomped on it?

401
00:17:59,810 --> 00:18:02,580
How hard did she stomp?

402
00:18:02,580 --> 00:18:04,580
Very hard.

403
00:18:04,580 --> 00:18:06,920
Okay   I'm good.

404
00:18:08,760 --> 00:18:10,960
Well   Raj

405
00:18:10,960 --> 00:18:14,360
I just want to say that I'd never betray your trust.

406
00:18:14,360 --> 00:18:16,930
Unlike Leonard   I respect you.

407
00:18:16,930 --> 00:18:17,930
Really?

408
00:18:17,930 --> 00:18:20,600
Mm-hmm.

409
00:18:20,600 --> 00:18:22,730
Was it out of respect that you didn't tell Raj

410
00:18:22,740 --> 00:18:25,370
about the time you dropped his iPhone in a urinal?

411
00:18:26,240 --> 00:18:29,510
Dude   I put that thing on my face!

412
00:18:29,510 --> 00:18:32,380
I think a more amusing violation of Raj's trust

413
00:18:32,380 --> 00:18:35,010
is when Howard convinced him that foreigners give presents

414
00:18:35,010 --> 00:18:37,950
to Americans on Thanksgiving.

415
00:18:38,820 --> 00:18:40,350
Hey   I didn't see you giving back

416
00:18:40,350 --> 00:18:43,190
your Snoopy snow cone maker.

417
00:18:43,190 --> 00:18:44,320
That was all a lie?

418
00:18:44,320 --> 00:18:46,460
This year's gifts are already wrapped.

419
00:18:46,460 --> 00:18:49,190
And as long as we're talking about betraying our friends

420
00:18:49,200 --> 00:18:51,660
how about the month Sheldon spent grinding up insects

421
00:18:51,660 --> 00:18:53,400
and mixing them into Leonard's food?

422
00:18:53,400 --> 00:18:54,770
Well   excuse me.

423
00:18:54,770 --> 00:18:56,370
That was not a betrayal.

424
00:18:56,370 --> 00:18:58,500
That was an experiment to determine

425
00:18:58,500 --> 00:19:02,710
at what concentration food starts tasting "mothy."

426
00:19:02,710 --> 00:19:05,880
You put moths in my food?!

427
00:19:06,710 --> 00:19:09,750
For science.

428
00:19:09,750 --> 00:19:12,220
I can't believe you kissed my sister with moth mouth.

429
00:19:12,220 --> 00:19:16,390
Well   I can't believe you used Sheldon's toothbrush.

430
00:19:16,390 --> 00:19:18,690
You used my toothbrush?

431
00:19:18,690 --> 00:19:21,590
Not the brush part   just the little rubber thing

432
00:19:21,590 --> 00:19:25,430
to pick food from my teeth and massage my gums.

433
00:19:31,070 --> 00:19:34,110
Okay   I-I think it's safe to say

434
00:19:34,110 --> 00:19:35,610
that we've all done some things

435
00:19:35,610 --> 00:19:37,380
we're not particularly proud of.

436
00:19:38,340 --> 00:19:39,540
But come on   we're friends.

437
00:19:39,550 --> 00:19:43,520
Friends overlook each other's minor lapses.

438
00:19:44,720 --> 00:19:47,520
For the record   Howard   I'm sorry that I broke our pact.

439
00:19:47,520 --> 00:19:49,860
Thank you.

440
00:19:49,860 --> 00:19:52,690
And I'm sorry about your phone

441
00:19:52,690 --> 00:19:54,490
and Thanksgiving.

442
00:19:54,490 --> 00:19:55,860
And while we're at it

443
00:19:55,860 --> 00:19:58,300
you don't have to wash our clothes on the Fourth of July.

444
00:19:59,770 --> 00:20:01,870
As long as we're apologizing

445
00:20:01,870 --> 00:20:05,100
Sheldon   I'm   I'm sorry I used your toothbrush.

446
00:20:05,100 --> 00:20:07,340
And I'm sorry...

447
00:20:07,340 --> 00:20:08,840
but that behavior is beyond the pale

448
00:20:08,840 --> 00:20:10,510
and cannot be tolerated.

449
00:20:10,510 --> 00:20:12,640
We are no longer friends.

450
00:20:12,650 --> 00:20:16,680
I got you a talking Thomas the Tank Engine for Thanksgiving.

451
00:20:16,680 --> 00:20:19,650
With real puffing smoke?

452
00:20:19,650 --> 00:20:20,890
Yes.

453
00:20:21,690 --> 00:20:23,220
All right.

454
00:20:25,530 --> 00:20:27,230
But I'm watching you.

455
00:20:39,270 --> 00:20:40,740
Hey   you've got Snoopy out.

456
00:20:40,740 --> 00:20:41,940
Can I have a snow cone?

457
00:20:41,940 --> 00:20:44,810
Well   sure.

458
00:20:46,750 --> 00:20:47,750
This is pretty good.

459
00:20:47,750 --> 00:20:49,020
What flavor is this?

460
00:20:49,020 --> 00:20:51,920
Guess.

461
00:20:51,920 --> 00:20:53,520
- Papaya? - No.

462
00:20:53,520 --> 00:20:56,160
- Guava? - You're so close.

463
00:20:56,160 --> 00:20:57,160
I give up.

464
00:20:57,160 --> 00:20:59,560
Mango caterpillar.

465
00:21:01,860 --> 00:21:02,730
What are you doing?!

466
00:21:04,470 --> 00:21:07,700
You said you liked it.

